WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.520
Draconian bills to restrict self-defense rights have a life of their own in Congress.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.900
There's always one lurking in the background. Left to its own devices, it's unlikely to become law,

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.960
but it's ready to be deployed if a suitable high-profile crime or a convenient crisis emerges

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:21.040
to ease its passage. And that brings us to the Gun Violence Prevention and Community Safety Act of 2020.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.860
A far-reaching bill hovering in the legislative shadows as the COVID-19 pandemic breaks down barriers

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:32.040
to authoritarian measures. Introduced in the Senate and the House at the end of January, by Senator

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.980
Elizabeth Warren of Massachusetts and Representative Hank Johnson of Georgia, the bill would impose

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.700
federal licensing for guns and ammunition, require universal background checks,

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:48.080
ban so-called assault weapons, outlaw normal capacity magazines, regulate DIY firearms,

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:53.320
and otherwise impose the full wish list of restrictions sought by those who would prefer to see

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:59.280
an armed government ruling over disarmed citizens. With its massive intrusions into rights cherished by

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.520
much of the population, the proposed law is a recipe for massive non-compliance,

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:09.140
confrontations between people and enforcers, and deepened political divisions. It's also exactly the

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:14.140
sort of legislation that is normally dead on arrival, but these aren't normal times.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:20.280
Officials with fever dreams of expanded power thrive on our fear. "As the Coronavirus pandemic brings the world

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.720
to a juddering halt, and anxious citizens
demand action, leaders across the globe

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.580
are invoking executive powers and
seizing virtually dictatorial authority

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:32.480
with scant resistance,"  The New York Times warned on March 30th.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:35.360
The restrictions described in the
article are wide-ranging covering

00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:38.820
everything from detaining people to
surveillance the censorship of speech

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:42.600
aimed at politicians and their policies
the Department of Justice has floated

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.610
the idea of indefinite detention
California governor Gavin Newsom

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:50.450
speculated about the possibility of
martial law if we feel the necessity

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:54.750
Washington DC's mayor Muriel Bowser
wants to arrest anybody who ventures

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:58.710
from home for an unapproved reason and
jurisdictions across the country have

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:02.310
ordered or considered ordering gun
stores along with other non-essential

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.899
businesses closed for the duration of
the crisis in selling their gun bill

00:02:06.899 --> 00:02:10.240
Warren and Johnson play on the fears of
many members of the public

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:15.670
and their desire to be saved from unseen
perils in a joint January 30th press

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:19.570
release trumpeting their gun bill Warren
and Johnson described a country rife

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:24.190
with violence in homes and on sidewalks
in schools and supermarkets in places of

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:28.540
worship and workplaces it invoked fear
of a false crisis involving a made-up

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:34.120
epidemic just as a real crisis sized
epidemic was rolling into our lives that

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:38.410
potent combination of real and overblown
crises doesn't mean that the gun

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:43.120
violence prevention and Community Safety
Act of 2020 will pass but it does mean

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.900
that this is a ripe moment for
authoritarian laws and practices of all

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:52.000
sorts it also means that this particular
legislative monstrosity is being sold in

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.350
precisely the most effective way for
such a moment and pushback is an

00:02:56.350 --> 00:03:00.550
important just for self-defense rights
it's a necessary part of a larger effort

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:05.200
to put government's on notice they must
stop exploiting our fear to expand their

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.500
power

